<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan tenders for up to 7,000 tonnes of Apr MTBE.</title>
<headline>Taiwan tenders for up to 7,000 tonnes of Apr MTBE.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) has issued a tender to buy its April requirement of methyl tertiary butyl ether (MTBE), a company official said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The tender, which seeks 3,500 tonnes to 7,000 tonnes of MTBE for April 6-20 delivery to Kaohsiung or Keelung, closes March 3 and is valid until March 5.</p>
<p>CPC last bought 7,000 tonnes of MTBE at around $283 per tonne on a cost-and-freight basis to Taiwan from Saudi Basic Industries Corp (SABIC).</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3086)</p>
